    "category": "Security",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-08-17",
    "body": "Miami International is the main gateway between the US, Latin America, and the Caribbean. American Airlines runs the hub, and the airport handles over 52 million passengers annually across a horseshoe-shaped terminal layout. TSA lines at MIA can stretch to 45 to 75 minutes during peak periods. Here's how to navigate them.\r\n\r\nBecause of heavy international passenger volume, high baggage loads, and weekend cruise passenger surges, TSA lines at MIA can stretch past **45–75 minutes** during peak departure banks.\r\n\r\nThis guide provides live security tracking tools, checkpoint breakdown across Concourses D through J, peak travel waves, and practical strategies to navigate Miami Airport security quickly.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## MIA TSA Wait Times Overview\r\n\r\n| Terminal & Concourse | Primary Airlines | Peak Standard Wait | TSA PreCheck Wait | CLEAR Available? |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **North Terminal (Concourse D)** | American Airlines Hub (Domestic & Intl) | 25–65 min | < 10 min | ✅ Yes (Checkpoints 1 & 2) |\r\n| **Central Terminal (Concourse E)** | American, British Airways, Qatar, Iberia | 20–50 min | < 10 min | ❌ No |\r\n| **Central Terminal (Concourse F/G)** | Cayman, Sunwing, Surinam, Volaris, WestJet | 20–45 min | < 10 min | ❌ No |\r\n| **South Terminal (Concourse H)** | Delta, Air France, KLM, Aeromexico | 25–55 min | < 10 min | ❌ No |\r\n| **South Terminal (Concourse J)** | United, Lufthansa, LATAM, Virgin Atlantic, Avianca | 30–70 min | < 10 min | ✅ Yes |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## How to Check Live MIA TSA Wait Times\r\n\r\nBefore taking the Dolphin Expressway (SR 836) or Metrorail to MIA, monitor real-time queue lengths:\r\n\r\n### 1. Miami International Airport Official Website\r\nVisit the official MIA security tracker at [miami-airport.com](https://www.miami-airport.com). MIA provides real-time estimated checkpoint wait times color-coded across all concourses.\r\n\r\n### 2. The Official MyTSA App\r\nThe **MyTSA app** (iOS/Android) gives travelers up-to-the-minute crowd estimates and historical wait trends for Miami International Airport.\r\n\r\n### 3. MIA Airport Mobile App (MIA Airport Official)\r\nAvailable on iOS and [Android](/items/smartphone/), the official MIA app features interactive maps and live wait time displays for each concourse checkpoint.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## MIA Concourse-by-Concourse Security Breakdown\r\n\r\nMiami's semi-circular terminal layout divides into three distinct zones:\r\n\r\n```\r\n            ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\r\n            │        MIAMI INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT (MIA)      │\r\n            │                                               │\r\n            │  [ NORTH TERMINAL ]     [ CENTRAL TERMINAL ]  │\r\n            │  Concourse D (AA Hub)   Concourses E, F, G    │\r\n            │  Checkpoints 1, 2, 3, 4                       │\r\n            │                                               │\r\n            │  [ SOUTH TERMINAL ]                           │\r\n            │  Concourse H (Delta/SkyTeam)                  │\r\n            │  Concourse J (United/Star "
