    "slug": "tsa-touchless-id-guide",
    "title": "TSA Confirm ID & Touchless ID: How TSA PreCheck Identity Verification Works",
    "description": "What is TSA Confirm ID and TSA Touchless ID? Learn how identity verification works at airport security, how IDEMIA TSA PreCheck fits in, and what to expect.",
    "category": "Security",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-08-17",
    "body": "TSA's identity verification process is changing. Two programs are now part of the airport experience at a growing number of checkpoints: TSA Touchless ID and TSA Confirm ID. Both use biometric technology to match your face to your ID, and both are worth understanding before you fly.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## TSA Confirm ID & Touchless ID: Summary\r\n\r\n| Feature | TSA Touchless ID | TSA Confirm ID |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| **What it does** | Biometric facial recognition at checkpoint | Identity verification for TSA PreCheck enrollment |\r\n| **Who uses it** | TSA PreCheck members at participating airports | Travelers enrolling in or renewing TSA PreCheck |\r\n| **Technology** | Facial recognition [cameras](/items/camera/) at TSA lanes | Secure online identity proofing |\r\n| **Required?** | Optional (you can opt out) | Required for PreCheck enrollment |\r\n| **Run by** | TSA | IDEMIA (TSA-authorized vendor) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## What Is TSA Touchless ID?\r\n\r\n**TSA Touchless ID** is a biometric facial recognition system deployed at select airport security checkpoints. Instead of manually handing your ID to a TSA officer for visual inspection, a camera captures your face and [matches](/items/matches/) it against your [passport](/items/passport/) or [driver's license](/items/drivers-license/) photo stored in government databases.\r\n\r\n### How TSA Touchless ID Works\r\n\r\n1. You approach the TSA document check station\r\n2. A camera captures your face automatically\r\n3. The system compares your face to your government-issued ID photo\r\n4. Verification is confirmed in seconds — the officer sees a green check\r\n5. You proceed normally through the security lane\r\n\r\n**TSA Touchless ID is currently available at:**\r\n- Select lanes at major hub airports (including LAX, JFK, DFW, IAH, and others)\r\n- TSA PreCheck dedicated lanes at participating airports\r\n\r\n### Can I Opt Out of TSA Touchless ID?\r\n\r\nYes. TSA Touchless ID / facial recognition is **optional**. You may decline the biometric scan and have your ID manually checked by the TSA officer. Simply tell the officer you prefer manual ID verification.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> Opting out of facial recognition does not affect your TSA PreCheck status. You will still be processed through the PreCheck lane; the officer will verify your ID manually.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## What Is TSA Confirm ID?\r\n\r\n**TSA Confirm ID** refers to the identity verification step in the TSA PreCheck enrollment and renewal process — particularly when done through IDEMIA's online portal.\r\n\r\n### IDEMIA and TSA PreCheck Identity Verification\r\n\r\n**IDEMIA** is one of two companies authorized by TSA to enroll travelers in TSA PreCheck. IDEMIA's enrollment process includes:\r\n\r\n1. **Online Application:** Complete your PreCheck application at IDEMIA's enrollment site (identogo.com)\r\n2. **Identity Confirmation:** You confirm your identity through document upload and a liveness check (selfie) OR at an in-person appointment\r\n3. **Fingerprinting:** A TSA-required fingerprint scan at the enrollment center\r\n4. **Backg"
