    "slug": "tsa-wait-times-guide",
    "title": "TSA Wait Times: How to Check Security Lines at IAH, LAX, JFK, DFW & More",
    "description": "How to check TSA wait times at any airport. Live wait time tools for IAH, LAX, JFK, DFW and all major US airports. Tips to avoid the longest security lines.",
    "category": "Security",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-08-17",
    "body": "TSA wait times can swing from 8 minutes to 90 minutes at the same airport depending on the time of day and day of the week. At major hubs like LAX, JFK, and DFW, bad timing during peak hours can make or break a connection. Here's how to check live wait times and how to avoid the worst lines.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## How to Check TSA Wait Times (Live)\r\n\r\n### 1. TSA's Official Wait Time Tool\r\nThe **TSA official website** at [tsa.gov/what-to-expect/wait-times](https://www.tsa.gov/what-to-expect/wait-times) shows crowd-sourced, self-reported wait times submitted by travelers at each checkpoint. These are updated throughout the day.\r\n\r\n### 2. MyTSA App (Official TSA Mobile App)\r\nThe **MyTSA app** (free, iOS and Android) shows:\r\n- Current estimated wait times by airport and terminal\r\n- Historical wait time patterns by hour and day\r\n- What you can and can't bring through security\r\n- Prohibited items checker\r\n\r\n### 3. Airport-Specific Apps & Websites\r\nMost major U.S. airports publish their own real-time security wait times:\r\n- **LAX:** flylax.com → \"Flights & Info\" → \"Security Wait Times\"\r\n- **JFK:** jfkairport.com → wait times by terminal\r\n- **DFW:** dfwairport.com → airport maps with wait time indicators\r\n- **IAH / George Bush Intercontinental:** fly2houston.com → live security wait data\r\n\r\n### 4. Google Search\r\nSearching **\"[airport code] tsa wait times\"** (e.g., \"IAH TSA wait times\" or \"JFK TSA wait times\") often surfaces real-time data cards directly in Google's search results, pulled from TSA's or the airport's data feeds.\r\n\r\n### 5. Third-Party Apps\r\n- **FlightAware** and **FlightRadar24** show gate/terminal information\r\n- **Google Maps** sometimes shows crowd levels at airport terminals\r\n- **iFly.com** aggregates security wait times and airport guides\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## IAH TSA Wait Times (George Bush Intercontinental Airport, Houston)\r\n\r\n**IAH** (George Bush Intercontinental Airport) is Houston's primary international hub and one of the busiest airports in the southern United States. It is served by **United Airlines** as a major hub.\r\n\r\n### IAH Security Checkpoints\r\n\r\nIAH has multiple terminals (A, B, C, D, E) each with their own TSA checkpoints. Wait times vary significantly by terminal:\r\n\r\n| Terminal | Primary Airlines | Typical Peak Wait |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Terminal A | United Airlines | 20–45 min |\r\n| Terminal B | United Airlines | 20–40 min |\r\n| Terminal C | United (international) | 30–60 min |\r\n| Terminal D | International arrivals | 25–50 min |\r\n| Terminal E | Domestic carriers | 15–35 min |\r\n\r\n### IAH TSA PreCheck Wait Times\r\nTSA PreCheck members at IAH typically wait **under 10 minutes** even during peak periods. PreCheck lanes are available in all terminals at IAH.\r\n\r\n### Best Times to Go Through IAH Security\r\n- **Lowest wait:** Weekday midday (10am–2pm), early morning (4:30–6am)\r\n- **Highest wait:** Friday afternoons, Sunday evenings, holiday periods\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## LAX TSA Wait Times (Los Angeles International Airport)\r\n\r\n**LAX** is one of the busiest ai"
