    "body": "[Tweezers](/items/tweezers/) are allowed in carry-on bags without restriction. Pack them, don't think twice. The only unlikely exception is extremely long, pointed tweezers, where an officer might use discretion, but that's genuinely rare with standard cosmetic tweezers.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## TSA Rules Summary\r\n\r\n- **Tweezers in Carry-On:** ✅ Allowed\r\n- **Tweezers in Checked Baggage:** ✅ Allowed\r\n- **TSA Declaration Required:** No\r\n- **International Travel:** Generally allowed (verify for specific destinations)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Official Regulations\r\n\r\n### Tweezers Are Allowed in Carry-On\r\n\r\nThe TSA explicitly lists tweezers as **permitted in carry-on baggage**. Standard cosmetic tweezers — whether slanted tip, pointed tip, flat tip, or rounded tip — are all allowed through the security checkpoint without restriction.\r\n\r\nThe TSA's position is that standard tweezers do not pose a meaningful security threat. They are classified alongside other permitted personal grooming tools.\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n> While TSA permits tweezers, individual TSA officers retain discretionary authority. In practice, tweezers are almost never flagged at checkpoints. However, very large, heavy, or unusually sharp tweezers may occasionally draw a second look.\r\n\r\n### What Types of Tweezers Are Allowed?\r\n\r\n| Tweezer Type | Carry-On | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Standard cosmetic tweezers | ✅ Allowed | Most common type — no issues |\r\n| Slant-tip tweezers | ✅ Allowed | |\r\n| Pointed-tip tweezers | ✅ Allowed | May get a closer look, but generally allowed |\r\n| Ingrown hair tweezers | ✅ Allowed | |\r\n| [Eyebrow tweezers](/items/tweezers/) | ✅ Allowed | |\r\n| Medical/surgical tweezers | ✅ Allowed | May require declaration if part of [medical kit](/items/first-aid-kit/) |\r\n| Large industrial tweezers | ⚠️ Officer discretion | Unusually large tools may be flagged |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Grooming Tools: What's Allowed vs. Prohibited\r\n\r\nSince you're packing tweezers, here's a quick reference for other common grooming tools:\r\n\r\n| Item | Carry-On | Checked |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Tweezers | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Nail clippers](/items/nail-clippers/) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| Nail file (metal) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| Scissors (blades under 4 inches) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| Scissors (blades 4 inches+) | ❌ Not allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Razors](/items/razor/) (disposable cartridge) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| Safety razor (with blade) | ❌ Not allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Straight razor](/items/safety-razor/) | ❌ Not allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Beard trimmer](/items/beard-trimmer/) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Electric shaver](/items/electric-razor/) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| [Curling iron](/items/curling-iron/) | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n| Hairdryer | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## International Rules for Tweezers\r\n\r\nMost international aviation authorities follow similar standards to TSA and permit tweezers in carry-on bags. However, some countries apply stricter definitions of \"sharp objects\":\r\n\r\n"
